{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Revised the description to address the plan-review BLOCK findings.\n\n- Final description length: 6,991 characters.\n- Concrete bridge now specified: `Claude Sonnet 4.5 (Amazon Bedrock Edition)` + `USE1-MP:USE1_InputTokenCount-Units` derives rate key `USE1-Claude Sonnet 4.5-input-tokens`; `_match()` normalises that body to `claudesonnet45`, compares it with model target `claudesonnet4520250929v10`, and relies on the existing `norm in target` substring branch.\n- Added key-pinning and end-to-end ACs requiring `rates[\"USE1-Claude Sonnet 4.5-input-tokens\"]` and `_rate_for(\"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0\", \"InputTokenCount\", rates)` returning that same empirical rate.\n- Split bundled ACs into 22 checkbox lines, each targeting one verifiable claim.\n- Removed the vague phrase `as needed`; structural checks now pass: `check_ac` reports 22 criteria lines, and `quality_check` reports 22 AC items with 2 file-impact paths.\n\nNo repository files were modified. No ticket claim, transition, plan review, completion verification, `make test`, or `make verify` was run. No background process was started."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789878165785144912,"uuid":"111cbb18-ceeb-4769-969c-a8123cde7a2b"}